# Tests

- Places: unit `src/test/openMarket/<layer>/<ctx>/<Name>.spec.js` (mocha + chai, ports faked with plain objects returning `Rx.Observable.of(...)`); integration `src/itest/<Ctx>Spec.js` (real container, temp SQLite under the OS temp dir); e2e `e2e/*.spec.js` (Playwright + Electron).
- Test data is built through the aggregates and use cases, never by raw SQL or by assigning `_fields`. Reuse helpers such as `src/test/openMarket/support/placedOrder.js`; a helper that can build an invalid aggregate is a bug.
- Time is a fake `Clock` passed in, never the real date.
- Assert behaviour the caller can see (returned values, saved aggregates, raised events, dispatched actions), not private calls.
- A changed `domain/` file needs its mutants killed (`om-finish` skill). Never weaken, skip or delete a test to pass a gate.
- Iterate with `npm test -- --reporter dot --grep "<Name>"`; e2e with `npx playwright test e2e/<name>.spec.js --reporter=line`. Layout e2e uses `setViewportSize` at 1024×700 and 1366×768.
